# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Root .gitattributes for the Contextle monorepo.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# --- Rank artifact roots (docs/ARTIFACT_FORMAT.md) ---
# These files are hash-verified data, not source. `vocabulary.txt` is the exact
# byte sequence whose sha256 `manifest.json` records, and the backend refuses a
# root whose vocabulary is not byte-identical to canonical form
# (backend/app/services/scoring/artifact/vocabulary.py).
#
# Git's autocrlf would rewrite it. `vocabulary.txt` is detected as text, so on a
# checkout with `core.autocrlf=true` — the Windows default, and what this repo is
# developed on — every one of its 59,582 lines gains a CR, the sha256 changes,
# and the server fails startup on a file nobody edited. `-text` disables that
# conversion in both directions, so the bytes committed are the bytes checked
# out on every platform.
#
# The `.npy` arrays are already detected as binary and pass through unchanged;
# they are covered anyway rather than left to a content heuristic.
#
# `binary` rather than a bare `-text` (it means `-text -diff -merge`), for two
# reasons beyond the byte preservation both give:
#
#   - `manifest.json` arrives from the producer with CRLF line endings. Those
#     bytes are part of the delivered artifact and are left alone, but a file
#     git still diffs as *text* reports every one of its CRs as trailing
#     whitespace — 83 spurious `git diff --check` errors on a file nobody is
#     going to hand-edit.
#   - Nothing here is reviewed by reading a diff. A changed root is verified by
#     its sha256 and by `load_manifest`, so a 59,582-line textual diff of
#     `vocabulary.txt` is noise in every review it ever appears in.
backend/artifacts/** binary
backend/artifacts/final/**/*.npy filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
